-- title:
--   Faithfulness of τ — ((trD ⊗ τ)(|P(s, s*)|^{2p}))^{1/2p} → ‖P(s, s*)‖
-- statement:
--   For every $P \in \mathrm M_D(\mathbb C) \otimes \mathbb C\langle \boldsymbol s, \boldsymbol s^*\rangle$,
--   $$\Big(\mathrm{Re}\,(\mathrm{tr}_D \otimes \tau)\big((P(\boldsymbol s, \boldsymbol s^*)^* P(\boldsymbol s, \boldsymbol s^*))^p\big)\Big)^{1/2p} \to \|P(\boldsymbol s, \boldsymbol s^*)\| \quad (p \to \infty),$$
--   where $\mathrm{tr}_D \otimes \tau$ is `StrongConv.trTau` and $\|\cdot\|$ is the operator norm on $D$ copies of $\ell^2(\mathbf F_d)$.
--
--   In the proof of Theorem A.1 of C.-F. Chen, J. Garza-Vargas, J. A. Tropp and R. van Handel, *A new approach to strong convergence*, Ann. of Math. (2) 203 (2026) 555–602 (arXiv v3, p. 33) this is stated as “$((\mathrm{tr}_D \otimes \tau)(|P(s, s^*)|^{2p}))^{1/2p} = \|P(s, s^*)\| - o(1)$ as $p \to \infty$ due to the fact that $\tau$ defines a faithful state on the $C^*$-algebra $C^*_{\mathrm{red}}(\mathbf F_d)$ that is generated by $s$ [54, Proposition 3.12]”. The reduced $C^*$-algebra enters through faithfulness of $\tau$: if $T \ge 0$ lies in $\mathrm M_D(\mathbb C) \otimes C^*_{\mathrm{red}}(\mathbf F_d)$ and $(\mathrm{tr}_D \otimes \tau)(T) = 0$, then $T = 0$, because $T$ commutes with the right translations of $\ell^2(\mathbf F_d)$.
-- source:
--   Chen, C.-F., Garza-Vargas, J., Tropp, J. A. and van Handel, R., A new approach to strong convergence, Ann. of Math. (2) 203 (2026) 555–602, https://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2026.203.2.4 (arXiv:2405.16026v3, whose page numbers are used), p. 33, proof of Theorem A.1 (faithfulness of tau)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_StrongConv

